        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Fetteresso Castle, Cowie Castle, Catterline, Aberdeenshire, Scotland\n- Buildings: Fiddes Castle, Chapel of St. Mary and St. Nathalan, Muchalls Castle\n- Concepts: towerhouse, Scottish gothic style Palladian manor, prehistoric use, ruined fortress\n\nFacts:\n- Fetteresso Castle is a 14th-century towerhouse.\n- Fetteresso Castle was rebuilt in 1761 as a Scottish gothic style Palladian manor.\n- The site of Fetteresso Castle shows clear evidence of prehistoric use.\n- Cowie Castle is a ruined fortress in Aberdeenshire, Scotland.\n- The general area of Catterline includes noted architectural or historic features such as Fetteresso Castle, Fiddes Castle, the Chapel of St. Mary and St. Nathalan, and Muchalls Castle.",
